    <briefdescription>
<para>Capacity limit exceeded error. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classcslt_1_1CapacityOverflowError" kindref="compound">CapacityOverflowError</ref> represents an error when a capacity policy or representable limit is exceeded.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example Usage:</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>CapacityOverflowError();<sp/><sp/>//<sp/>&quot;Capacity<sp/>limit<sp/>exceeded&quot;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">throw<sp/>CapacityOverflowError(&quot;Container<sp/>capacity<sp/>cannot<sp/>exceed<sp/>65535<sp/>elements&quot;);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
